-- Color.cm -- Gargoyle, the 1986 colour illustrator, on the colour display.-- Gargoyle is Griffin's successor and the ancestor of the one in the Cedar 13-- screenshots; its load file is signed by Ken Pier and Eric Bier.Echo Turning the colour display on...ColorDisplay onEcho Fetching Gargoyle and its eleven imported packages. This is a bigEcho closure, so give it several minutes.Bringover -p [Cedar]<CedarChest6.1>Top>Gargoyle.df-- BiScrollers FIRST, and this line is the whole reason Gargoyle would not-- start. The user profile loads BiScrollers from CedarChest6.0 at BOOT, but-- Gargoyle is a 6.1 build, so Run Gargoyle.bcd died on-- VersionMismatch[BiScrollers]. That meant no Gargoyle command was ever-- registered, hence the .load file failed to register command and no window.-- The Bringover above has already put 6.1's BiScrollers BCDs in the working-- directory; running them augments the system with the newer version, which-- is Cedar's own idiom for exactly this situation.Echo Loading the 6.1 BiScrollers so Gargoyle can bind to it...Run Geom2DImpl BiScrollersImpl BiScrollersButtonnedEcho Loading Gargoyle, its packages, and the ColorTool...Source Gargoyle.loadEcho Now type  Gargoyle  to open it, pick colours from the ColorTool, draw aEcho shape, and drag the viewer onto the colour screen.